id: pm-te6elw
title: "SDK completeness is asserted by a 10-case curated array against 85 declared actions: the boundary proves the CLI reaches nothing below the SDK, nothing proves the SDK can do what the CLI does"
description: "Verified 2026-07-26: src/cli has zero imports below the SDK (downward containment proven by pm-9x6e), but PM_TOOL_ACTIONS declares 85 actions while action-schema-parity.spec.ts curates 10 literal cases, so 75 actions are unasserted and a new command with no SDK action keeps the suite green. ADR pm-w13j already ruled the curated form unacceptable for completeness gates. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched SDK-parity/promotion/boundary/ratchet items across all statuses; pm-9x6e and pm-8778 own downward containment, pm-e6tm5c freezes the export surface, pm-cbwg and pm-w89s proved the exemplar once. No item gates upward completeness continuously."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: architecture,"area:cli","area:contracts","area:sdk",ci-gate,ratchet,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-07-26T05:44:44.266Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T14:09:09.776Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "The curated SCHEMA_PARITY_CASES array is replaced by a gate deriving its subjects from the command registry, so every declared action is examined without anyone maintaining a list; the gate asserts three separately-reported properties — action completeness (every dispatchable action has an SDK entry point), bidirectional parameter completeness (every flag maps to a schema parameter and every parameter is reachable from a flag), and behavioural equivalence over declared representative invocations at the result-envelope level; behavioural equivalence is enforced as a committed shrinking-only ratchet rather than as a false claim of exhaustiveness; rendering, help layout, colour and pager behaviour are explicitly excluded and the boundary is documented as the result envelope, not the rendered bytes; a negative-control fixture registering a command with no SDK action proves the gate fails, per pm-k6t4yb; each of the 75 currently unasserted actions ends up covered by the derived gate, covered by the ratchet, or carrying a recorded waiver with a stated reason; the gate runs in the existing static gate matrix beside sdk:surface:check and contracts:check"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Every capability the CLI can dispatch is provably reachable from the public SDK, checked continuously rather than demonstrated once"
value: The universal-tool claim stops depending on a point-in-time exemplar; a command that adds behaviour the SDK cannot reach fails the build instead of quietly widening the gap
why_now: "The import boundary is at zero and reads as if SDK-first is finished, which makes the remaining asymmetry invisible; 49,643 lines live in src/cli and nothing measures how much of it an SDK consumer can reproduce"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
